1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,820
Are you a tea drinker?
你是一名茶饮爱好者吗？

2
00:00:02,820 --> 00:00:05,470
If so, you’re not alone.
如果是的话，你并不是一个人。

3
00:00:05,470 --> 00:00:14,740
Every day around the world millions of cups of this popular brew are drunk, and it’s been that way for thousands of years.
在全球范围内，每天都有上百万杯这种广受欢迎的饮品被人们饮用，这样的习惯已经延续了数千年。

4
00:00:14,740 --> 00:00:24,200
The oldest discovered tea is from the Han Dynasty, dating from 206BC to 220AD.
目前发现的最古老的茶叶来自公元前206年至公元220年的汉朝。

5
00:00:24,200 --> 00:00:34,450
But it’s thought that the tea trend really took off during the Tang Dynasty in the 8th Century, when it became China’s national drink.
但人们认为，饮茶的风潮真正盛行起来是在公元8世纪的唐朝，当时茶成了中国的国饮。

6
00:00:34,450 --> 00:00:43,550
Now, Turkey, the Republic of Ireland and the UK are believed to be the biggest tea-drinking nations, per capita.
如今，土耳其、爱尔兰共和国和英国被认为是全球人均饮茶量最高的国家。

7
00:00:43,550 --> 00:00:50,760
Tea is consumed in many ways – slurped, sipped or glugged.
茶的饮用方式多种多样——可大口啜饮、小口抿饮，也可豪饮。

8
00:00:50,760 --> 00:01:00,740
It can be poured from pots, infused or brewed in the cup using tea bags – and it’s this latter process that is causing concern.
茶可以从茶壶中倒出饮用，也可以用茶包在杯中冲泡——而正是这后一种冲泡方式引发了人们的担忧。

9
00:01:00,740 --> 00:01:11,280
Research last year found some premium tea bags might be leaving billions of microscopic plastic particles in the cup.
去年的一项研究发现，一些高端茶包可能会在杯中留下数十亿个微小的塑料颗粒。

10
00:01:11,280 --> 00:01:21,500
Scientists from McGill University in Montreal found that some ‘plastic’ tea bags shed high levels of microplastics into water.
蒙特利尔麦吉尔大学的科学家们发现，一些“塑料材质”的茶包会向水中释放大量微塑料。

11
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:30,230
However, The World Health Organization says such particles in drinking water do not appear to pose a risk.
不过，世界卫生组织表示，饮用水中的这类塑料颗粒似乎并不会构成健康威胁。

12
00:01:30,230 --> 00:01:38,870
Most tea bags are made from paper, with a small amount of plastic used to seal them shut – made from oil.
大多数茶包的材质是纸，会使用少量以石油为原料制成的塑料来封口。

13
00:01:38,870 --> 00:01:46,140
This has led to debate about whether they can be recycled, but many are still composted.
这引发了关于茶包能否回收利用的争论，但许多茶包仍会被用于堆肥。

14
00:01:46,140 --> 00:01:58,910
However, gardener Mike Armitage has told the BBC that the plastic contained in the soil could be washed into streams and rivers and ultimately out to sea.
不过，园丁迈克·阿米蒂奇向英国广播公司表示，混入土壤中的塑料可能会被冲刷到小溪和河流中，最终流入大海。

15
00:01:58,910 --> 00:02:11,740
Unilever, the owners of the tea brand PG Tips, said their tea bags are made with a small amount of plastic – used to seal them – and that they are suitable for composting.
联合利华集团是茶饮品牌PG Tips的母公司，该集团表示，旗下茶包仅使用少量塑料用于封口，且这些茶包适合堆肥处理。

16
00:02:11,740 --> 00:02:24,300
And the brand Yorkshire Tea said their bags do contain 25% polypropylene, but they were “actively developing plant-based and biodegradable alternatives”.
约克郡茶品牌则称，其茶包确实含有25%的聚丙烯成分，但该品牌“正在积极研发植物基且可生物降解的替代品”。

17
00:02:24,300 --> 00:02:41,880
While tea bag manufacturers might be doing their bit to reduce plastic pollution, it could be a good time to switch your favourite beverage to coffee, or if that isn’t your cup of tea then try using loose-leaf tea, which can have a better flavour.
尽管茶包制造商们在为减少塑料污染尽自己的一份力，但或许现在是时候把你最爱的饮品换成咖啡了；如果你对咖啡不感兴趣，那么不妨试试散装茶叶，它的口感会更好。
